        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Rotten egg water is hydrogen sulfide, and the hot and cold tap test tells you where it is coming from. Hot only means the water heater and usually a new anode. Hot and cold on a well means bacteria or sulfur in the groundwater, and a water test decides between shock chlorination and continuous treatment. On city water, suspect your own equipment or a drain first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Fix the source rather than masking the smell, never leave a water heater without an anode, and take any sulfur smell in the air as a possible gas leak. If your well needs continuous treatment, our <a href="/best-water-filtration-system-for-home/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best whole-home water filtration systems</a> guide is the place to compare options.
